  "about": "Everyday words and phrases, mapped to the app's theme vocabulary so search can reach a passage from how someone actually feels. This is DATA, not code: anyone can add a line. Each key is a word or short phrase someone might type; each value lists the themes it should reach (spelled exactly as the passage theme tags are, e.g. \"Worry\", \"Provision\"). Multi-word phrases are matched whole and beat their individual words, so \"worried about money\" reaches worry and money, not every theme those words touch separately. You do not need to list a theme's own name (\"courage\" already finds Courage) — only the plainer words people reach for instead.",
